{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 30,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The words of Agur the son of Jakeh, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the prophecy: the man spoke to Ithiel, even to Ithiel and Ucal,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " more brutish than ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " man, and have not the understanding of a man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I neither learned wisdom, nor have the knowledge of the holy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath ascended into heaven, or descended? who hath gathered the wind in his fists? who hath bound the waters in a garment? who hath established all the ends of the earth? what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his name, and what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his son's name, if thou canst tell?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every word of God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pure: he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a shield to them that put their trust in him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Add thou not to his words, lest he reprove thee, and thou be found a liar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Two ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " have I required of thee; deny ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not to me before I die:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remove far from me vanity and lies; give me neither poverty nor riches; feed me with food convenient for me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lest I be full, and deny ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and say, Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD? or lest I be poor, and steal, and take the name of my God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in vain",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Accuse not a servant to his master, lest he curse thee, and thou be found guilty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a generation ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " curseth their father, and doth not bless their mother.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a generation ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pure in their own eyes, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " are not washed from their filthiness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a generation, O how lofty are their eyes! and their eyelids are lifted up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a generation, whose teeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " swords, and their jaw-teeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " knives, to devour the poor from off the earth, and the needy from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "among",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The horse-leech hath two daughters, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "crying",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", Give, give. There are three ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " are never satisfied, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yes",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", four ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " say not, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " enough:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The grave; and the barren womb; the earth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is not filled with water; and the fire ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " saith not, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " enough.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The eye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mocketh at ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "its",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " father, and despiseth to obey ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "its",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mother, the ravens of the valley shall pick it out, and the young eagles shall eat it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There are three ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " are too wonderful for me, yes, four which I know not:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The way of an eagle in the air; the way of a serpent upon a rock; the way of a ship in the midst of the sea; and the way of a man with a maid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Such ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the way of an adulterous woman; she eateth, and wipeth her mouth, and saith, I have done no wickedness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For three ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the earth is disquieted, and for four ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it cannot bear:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For a servant when he reigneth; and a fool when he is filled with food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For an odious ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "woman",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " when she is married; and a handmaid that is heir to her mistress.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There are four ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things which are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " little upon the earth, but they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " very wise:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The ants ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a people not strong, yet they prepare their food in the summer;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The conies ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a feeble people, yet they make their houses in the rocks;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The locusts have no king, yet go they forth all of them by bands;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The spider taketh hold with her hands, and is in king's palaces.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There are three ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which go well, yes, four are comely in going:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A lion, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strongest among beasts, and turneth not away for any;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A greyhound; a he-goat also; and a king, against whom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no rising up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou hast done foolishly in lifting up thyself, or if thou hast thought evil, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "lay",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy hand upon thy mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.30.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.30.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely the churning of milk bringeth forth butter, and the wringing of the nose bringeth forth blood: so the forcing of wrath bringeth forth strife.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
